WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.200 --> 00:00:04.380
American Horror Story has never shied away
from tackling controversial topics.

00:00:04.760 --> 00:00:09.480
The hit FX show will do whatever it takes
it torment, terrorize, and tantalize you,

00:00:09.480 --> 00:00:12.000
and needless to say, things get extreme.

00:00:12.240 --> 00:00:16.320
Here are some of the most controversial American
Horror Story moments of all time.

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.300
Season one of American Horror Story is full
of twisted violence that's become the show's

00:00:21.300 --> 00:00:26.160
stock in trade ... but there's one moment
that's always stood out as particularly shocking.

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:30.960
In the episode "Piggy Piggy," we see Tate
Langdon — played by Evan Peters — carrying

00:00:30.960 --> 00:00:34.820
out a school shooting and gunning down 15
of his fellow students.

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:38.380
“Dude, go!"

00:00:39.460 --> 00:00:44.220
The on-screen massacre gave many viewers flashbacks
to the horrific tragedy at Columbine High

00:00:44.220 --> 00:00:45.820
School in 1999.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:49.040
After the episode aired, The Atlantic's Richard
Lawson wrote,

00:00:49.260 --> 00:00:54.840
"It's more than a little tasteless in a 'Hey,
this, y'know, actually happened' kind of way.

00:00:54.840 --> 00:00:59.050
Obviously everything on the show, if done
in real life, is insanely terrible [...] but

00:00:59.050 --> 00:01:02.540
this particular set piece seemed so deliberately
exact.

00:01:02.740 --> 00:01:07.460
There was a particular event, or events, that
they were trying to directly evoke and that's

00:01:07.460 --> 00:01:08.460
just cruel."

00:01:09.140 --> 00:01:14.000
Set in the 1960s, the second season of American
Horror Story takes us to the fictional mental

00:01:14.000 --> 00:01:19.420
health facility Briarcliff Manor, and one
of its patients really outraged some viewers.

00:01:19.780 --> 00:01:20.640
"What's your name?

00:01:21.420 --> 00:01:24.700
I hear you caused quite a disturbance tonight.

00:01:25.120 --> 00:01:28.420
Some anti-Semitic remark set you off."

00:01:29.100 --> 00:01:33.560
In the episode "I Am Anne Frank - Part 1,"
a woman claiming to be Anne Frank shows up

00:01:33.560 --> 00:01:36.520
at Briarcliff, and some people just weren't
having it.

00:01:36.740 --> 00:01:39.200
Rolling Stone scribe Halle Kiefer wrote that:

00:01:39.320 --> 00:01:43.749
"Next time we see her, the woman is writing
in her journal in the Briarcliff common room.

00:01:43.749 --> 00:01:45.140
Because she’s Anne Frank.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:46.820
Her journal is even named Kitty.

00:01:46.980 --> 00:01:49.460
Oh lord, Anne Frank was a real person.

00:01:49.469 --> 00:01:50.569
It just isn’t done!

00:01:50.569 --> 00:01:52.300
Am I being too delicate about this?"

00:01:52.960 --> 00:01:56.689
Some viewers argued that the show was never
trying to depict the real Anne Frank, but

00:01:56.689 --> 00:01:59.700
rather a mentally ill woman who merely thought
she was Anne Frank.

00:02:00.149 --> 00:02:04.060
Ryan Murphy worked that angle in an interview
with Entertainment Weekly, claiming:

00:02:04.060 --> 00:02:07.899
"The Anne Frank thing was always interesting
to me because after the war […] there were

00:02:07.899 --> 00:02:12.260
many women who came forward after that diary
and said, 'Well I'm the real Anne Frank,'

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:13.620
and they were struck down.

00:02:13.900 --> 00:02:17.320
Many of them were found to be mentally ill
and suffering from schizophrenia."

00:02:18.100 --> 00:02:22.180
Plenty of people took issue with a scene in
Hotel, the fifth season of American Horror

00:02:22.180 --> 00:02:22.680
Story.

00:02:22.880 --> 00:02:27.459
In the season premiere, a heroin addict named
named Gabriel checks into the Hotel Cortez

00:02:27.460 --> 00:02:29.799
and soon suffers a terrible fate.

00:02:30.180 --> 00:02:30.980
"You know what?

00:02:31.420 --> 00:02:32.660
It's your lucky day.

00:02:33.340 --> 00:02:35.060
Mama's feeling magnanimous."

00:02:36.340 --> 00:02:40.640
Shortly after he gets to his room, Gabriel
has a horrific encounter with the Addiction

00:02:40.640 --> 00:02:44.640
Demon, a monstrous entity with some sadistic
sexual appetites.

00:02:44.900 --> 00:02:50.400
After watching the scene, Cosmopolitan's Danielle
Henderson was absolutely beside herself, writing

00:02:50.400 --> 00:02:50.900
that,

00:02:51.020 --> 00:02:53.840
"To say this scene was disturbing is an understatement."

00:02:54.300 --> 00:02:59.340
Conservative watchdog group Parents Television
Council sharply criticized the episode, claiming

00:02:59.340 --> 00:02:59.840
that,

00:02:59.980 --> 00:03:04.100
"[It's an] unbelievably explicit combination
of sex and violence."

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.220
Honestly, it's hard to argue with that one.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:10.260
In a letter to subscribers, PTC president
Tim Winter wrote that,

00:03:10.260 --> 00:03:15.000
"[The episode features the] most vile and
shocking content I've ever seen on TV.

00:03:15.000 --> 00:03:15.500
Ever.

00:03:15.620 --> 00:03:20.960
Most Americans have no idea this is primetime
fare on advertiser-supported basic cable.

00:03:20.960 --> 00:03:24.140
And everyone is paying for it as part of their
program bundle."

00:03:24.660 --> 00:03:27.360
Who knew The Church of Satan could be so sensitive?

00:03:27.840 --> 00:03:31.659
Members of the organization were reportedly
quite unhappy with the way the church's late

00:03:31.660 --> 00:03:35.000
founder was portrayed on American Horror Story:
Apocalypse.

00:03:35.249 --> 00:03:39.500
Known to his followers as the Black Pope,
Anton LaVey created the Church of Satan in

00:03:39.500 --> 00:03:43.860
the swinging '60s, using the sexual liberation
of the day to his advantage.

00:03:44.189 --> 00:03:49.040
His black masses could be unusually glitzy
affairs, attracting the likes of Sammy Davis

00:03:49.040 --> 00:03:51.540
Jr., Liberace, and Jayne Mansfield.

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:56.459
Well, one particularly memorable scene in
American Horror Story: Apocalypse features

00:03:56.460 --> 00:04:00.580
LaVey - portrayed by actor Carlo Rota - committing
a human sacrifice.

00:04:00.880 --> 00:04:03.920
Suffice to say, some Satanists were seriously
steamed.

00:04:05.600 --> 00:04:08.400
In a tweet posted to the Church of Satan's
official Twitter account, the organization

00:04:08.400 --> 00:04:08.900
said,

00:04:08.900 --> 00:04:13.980
"Anton LaVey didn't believe in Christ or an
Anti-Christ and sacrifice plays no role in

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:14.480
Satanism.

00:04:14.680 --> 00:04:19.200
Lazy writers appropriated his name and image
for their Devil worship drivel [which] is

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:20.900
unimpressive and boring."

00:04:21.440 --> 00:04:25.860
In the sixth episode of Cult — the seventh
season of American Horror Story — a crazed

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:29.740
cult leader played by Evan Peters stages a
massacre at his own rally.

00:04:34.580 --> 00:04:35.600
"Drop the gun!"

00:04:36.660 --> 00:04:40.660
It would be a divisive scene in the best of
times, but the episode aired shortly after

00:04:40.660 --> 00:04:41.880
a real-life shooting.

00:04:42.020 --> 00:04:47.360
On the night of October 1st, 2017, the deadliest
mass shooting in modern American history took

00:04:47.360 --> 00:04:48.520
place in Las Vegas.

00:04:48.940 --> 00:04:52.960
The AHS episode featuring the bloody rally
scene aired on October 10th.

00:04:53.400 --> 00:04:58.120
In reaction to the tragedy, the violent sequence
was re-edited and significantly toned down,

00:04:58.120 --> 00:05:00.640
but it was still a controversial moment of
television.

00:05:00.960 --> 00:05:04.340
The night the episode aired, the AV Club's
Molly Horan wrote:

00:05:04.500 --> 00:05:08.760
"The need to edit out a moment of violence
that now feels all too real is all the more

00:05:08.760 --> 00:05:13.250
chilling when you consider Cult is acting
as a giant metaphor (and some could say, as

00:05:13.250 --> 00:05:15.900
a giant mirror held up to) the post-election
era."

00:05:16.580 --> 00:05:17.780
Yeah, this was a first.

00:05:18.190 --> 00:05:22.780
Coven, the third season of American Horror
Story, featured what we'll go ahead and call

00:05:22.780 --> 00:05:28.580
"a tender moment" between the witch Queenie
- portrayed by Gabourey Sidibe - and a Minotaur

00:05:28.820 --> 00:05:31.440
Following the episode, the Daily Mail asked
its readership:

00:05:31.940 --> 00:05:35.200
"Is this the most horrific episode of American
Horror Story yet?

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:39.740
Even die-hard fans left shocked as [...] bestiality
take[s] centre stage"

00:05:39.980 --> 00:05:43.620
While that might be overstating it, the scene
is a bit much.

00:05:44.020 --> 00:05:45.040
"You just wanted love.

00:05:46.160 --> 00:05:47.460
And that makes you a beast?"

00:05:49.460 --> 00:05:54.400
Even if Minotaur sex isn't your particular
cup of tea, perhaps it's best to keep an open

00:05:54.400 --> 00:05:54.900
mind.

00:05:55.100 --> 00:05:58.340
After all, it sounds like Sidibe was totally
down with the scene.

00:05:58.340 --> 00:06:00.050
In fact, she told Parade magazine:

00:06:00.400 --> 00:06:04.900
"I knew to say yes and to step out with faith
and trust in Ryan and his entire production

00:06:04.900 --> 00:06:05.400
team.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:07.160
I took the Minotaur by the horns."

00:06:07.440 --> 00:06:09.140
Hey, to each their own, right?

